  "notes": "Drawn from 2020–2025 photos (Commons has no newer one of the scheme; the airframe category's own 2013–2015 photos show N916NN in American's old polished scheme, so the Reno Air paint postdates them: worth checking the airframe's 2014 'from'). The teal tail section's extent on the lower aft fuselage and under the tail cone is read from one photo from below and is a low-confidence guess at its lower edge; the belly wasn't seen clearly. No 'Reno Air' titles seen anywhere. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the title and Flight Symbol measured against the doors on N916NN (2021-11-03, right side): 'American' x 0.213-0.331, the symbol at 0.198, both further aft than first drawn (the same place as on the AirCal and TWA 737s); the cheatline's rise at the nose and the teal tail section's sweep drawn as curves.",
